    {
      "name": "section_faq",
      "value": "FAQ"
    },
    {
      "name": "section_guide",
      "value": "User Guide"
    },
    {
      "name": "faq1_title",
      "value": "How to add a two-step verification token?"
    },
    {
      "name": "faq1_subtitle",
      "value": "Scan, recognize from album, or enter secret manually"
    },
    {
      "name": "faq1_answer",
      "value": "There are three ways: 1. Scan QR code — tap the + button and choose \"Scan QR code\". 2. From album — import a QR screenshot via the album. 3. Manual entry — fill in issuer, account and secret. 💡 Tip: scanning is recommended"
    },
    {
      "name": "faq2_title",
      "value": "What is the difference between TOTP and HOTP?"
    },
    {
      "name": "faq2_subtitle",
      "value": "Time-based vs counter-based"
    },
    {
      "name": "faq2_answer",
      "value": "TOTP (Time-based OTP) generates codes based on the current time and refreshes every 30 or 60 seconds. HOTP (HMAC-based OTP) is counter-based and requires a manual trigger to increment after each use. Most services use TOTP."
    },
    {
      "name": "faq3_title",
      "value": "How to back up token data?"
    },
    {
      "name": "faq3_subtitle",
      "value": "Export an encrypted backup file for safe storage"
    },
    {
      "name": "faq3_answer",
      "value": "Go to Settings > Export Encrypted Backup, set a backup password and export the .o2fah file. Store the backup file in a safe place. Regular backups are recommended to prevent data loss."
    },
    {
      "name": "faq4_title",
      "value": "Is biometric lock secure?"
    },
    {
      "name": "faq4_subtitle",
      "value": "Local encryption + system-level biometric protection"
    },
    {
      "name": "faq4_answer",
      "value": "O2FAH uses HarmonyOS system-level biometric APIs, and all data is stored in an encrypted local area. Secrets are protected by the system secure area and are never uploaded to the cloud or shared with other apps."
    },
    {
      "name": "faq5_title",
      "value": "How to migrate data after changing phones?"
    },
    {
      "name": "faq5_subtitle",
      "value": "Export on the old phone, import on the new one"
    },
    {
      "name": "faq5_answer",
      "value": "On the old phone: Settings > Export Encrypted Backup. On the new phone, install O2FAH: Settings > Import Encrypted Backup, select the backup file and enter the password to restore all tokens."
    },
    {
      "name": "guide1_title",
      "value": "Quick Start Guide"
    },
    {
      "name": "guide1_content",
      "value": "O2FAH is a two-step verification (2FA) token manager compatible with TOTP and HOTP.\n\n1. Add token: tap the + button at the bottom-right of the home page to scan a QR code, recognize from album, or enter the secret manually.\n\n2. View codes: the token card shows the current code and remaining validity in real time; tap the card to quickly copy the code.\n\n3. Organize: filter by category tags, long-press to drag and reorder, swipe left to edit/delete tokens."
    },
    {
      "name": "guide2_title",
      "value": "How to use category tags"
    },
    {
      "name": "guide2_content",
      "value": "Tags help you organize and find tokens.\n\n1. Create: create custom tags in Settings > Manage Tags, with a name and color.\n\n2. Assign: select one or more tags when editing a token.\n\n3. Filter: the tag bar at the top of the home page filters by category; tap \"All\" to show all tokens."
    },
    {
      "name": "guide3_title",
      "value": "Backup & Restore Guide"
    },
    {
      "name": "guide3_content",
      "value": "Back up your token data regularly to prevent loss.\n\n1. Export: Settings > Export Encrypted Backup, set a password to generate an encrypted .o2fah file; store it somewhere safe (e.g. computer or cloud drive).\n\n2. Restore: on a new device open Settings > Import Encrypted Backup, select the backup file and enter the password to restore all tokens.\n\n3. Reminder: enable periodic backup reminders in settings to avoid forgetting."
    },
